From c4932e53c3aee73c44830a5080e641aad4b16fa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fokko Pieter Beekhof <fpbeekhof@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:17:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] elanmoc2: Fix protocol handling for 04f3:0c00 and restore
 delete

Tested on an HP Pavilion 14-ec0xxx (04f3:0c00, firmware 2.81) with the
example programs and with fprintd 1.94.3: enroll, verify, no-match,
cancel, delete and clear storage.

Protocol fixes, each checked against the sensor:

- The finger info reply is 70 bytes (2-byte header + 68-byte user ID),
  not 64. Reading 64 left 6 bytes queued on the command endpoint, which
  were then taken as the reply to the next command. Read 70, accept short
  replies and validate them: before a finger has been identified the
  sensor answers with just 40 ff.
- The sensor never replies to the abort command. Waiting for a reply left
  a read pending for 10 s that swallowed the reply to the next command
  after every cancel or close. Send abort on its own, outside the command
  state machine, and synchronously on close.
- The number reported on identify is not always the number a print was
  committed under, which is the one delete needs: a print committed as 1
  on an otherwise empty sensor is identified as 0 and can only be deleted
  as 1. When replacing an already enrolled finger, try each number (a
  wrong one is refused without side effects) instead of wiping the whole
  sensor when the first attempt fails, and match prints on the user ID
  only.
- If the sensor refuses the number chosen for a new print (40 ff at stage
  0, without waiting for a finger), move on to the next one.

Behaviour fixes:

- A finger the sensor does not know (0xfd) is a plain "no match" on
  verify/identify, not FP_DEVICE_ERROR_DATA_NOT_FOUND.
- 0xfd during enroll is a retry; previously the enrollment was completed
  with a retry-domain error and the freed state machine was then used.
- Report at most one result per verify/identify action: complete after a
  retry instead of waiting for another touch, use FPI_MATCH_ERROR for
  retries and do not free the reported error a second time.
- Commands that wait for a finger have no receive deadline; they end on a
  touch or on cancellation (was 10 s).
- A failed or cancelled send no longer leaves a command marked as in
  flight.
- Fix a one-byte overflow when copying the user ID.
- Do not delete prints that were not stored by libfprint (e.g. Windows
  Hello) when the same finger is enrolled again; fail with
  FP_DEVICE_ERROR_DATA_DUPLICATE instead.

Restore dev_class->delete: the sensor deletes a print given the number it
was committed under and its user ID, both of which are stored in the
print, and does not require a prior identify.

Listing stays unsupported: finger info is only available after a finger
has been identified, and on this firmware it ignores the requested index.

Not covered: the other product IDs claimed by the driver were not
available for testing, and tests/elanmoc2 has not been re-recorded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
